etails: >\n128\t      Extreme C structures: near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal.\n129\t      Characterize when bias becomes catastrophic across topologies.\n130\t      Identify structural conditions (spectral gap, diagonal dominance ratio)\n131\t      that predict bias severity — candidate features for practitioners.\n132\t\n133\t  # =============================================\n134\t  # Software / Reproducibility\n135\t  # =============================================\n136\t\n137\t  - id: plan_010\n138\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n139\t    description: \"annot-sensitivity Python toolkit (open-source release)\"\n140\t    priority: P1\n141\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n142\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_004, plan_007]\n143\t    details: >\n144\t      Package: user-specified DAG + confusion matrix(es) + downstream estimate →\n145\t      bias expressions (scalar K≤3, matrix K>3 with interpretability) +\n146\t      ASV bounds + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic plots.\n147\t      pip-installable, with worked examples for each topology.\n148\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0eb24f23-8763-4c5c-8a44-826ae89e20cd","uuid":"da1062f7-324e-4130-b1ea-a545ff19c1f6","timestamp":"2026-05-20T07:40:56.479Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod_0510/projects/causal_annot_error_attrib/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # =============================================\n  # Claim 1: Multi-class bias taxonomy\n  # =============================================\n\n  - id: plan_001\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Derive and MC-validate bias expressions for 6 DAG topologies with K=3\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: []\n    registry_id: null  # MVP confounding DAG = art_20260520_f08c30 (1/6 done)\n    details: >\n      For each topology (confounding, mediation, collider, M-bias, instrument, front-door):\n      derive closed-form K=3 bias expression, validate with MC (1000 reps × N=10000,\n      6 confusion matrix structures including near-permutation extreme).\n      Key question: which topologies show direction reversal under non-differential error?\n      Confounding already validated in MVP (no reversal, monotonic toward OVB).\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Extend bias expressions to K=5,7 — matrix notation + interpretability tools\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    details: >\n      Matrix-form expressions for general K. Three interpretability tools:\n      (a) eigendecomposition summaries identifying dominant bias modes,\n      (b) worst-case scalar bounds collapsing matrix to conservative scalar,\n      (c) diagnostic visualizations mapping confusion matrix regions to bias magnitude.\n      Validate on confounding + mediation + collider DAGs with K=5,7.\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Empirical confusion matrices: 3 LLMs × 3 CSS tasks vs gold-standard\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    api_cost_estimate: \"$300-550\"\n    deps: []\n    details: >\n      Tasks: protest event coding (K=5, ACLED/GPT-RE), stance detection (K=3, SemEval/VAST),\n      toxicity (K=2, as special case / consistency check, Civil Comments).\n      Models: Llama 4 Maverick (Together.ai), Qwen 3.5 Plus (OpenRouter), DeepSeek V4 (DeepSeek API).\n      ~30K annotations per model × 3 datasets × 3 prompt variants.\n      Output: empirical confusion matrices, inter-model correlation analysis,\n      downstream regression bias vs gold-standard baseline.\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Binarization collapse analysis: K→2 folding bias across all 6 topologies\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    details: >\n      For each of 6 topologies with K=3,5,7: collapse to binary, compare bias\n      from full multi-class expression vs binarized expression.\n      Demonstrate that binarization is not a safe shortcut — can amplify or reverse bias.\n      MVP showed Δ up to 0.089 for confounding DAG K=3.\n\n  # =============================================\n  # Claim 2: Annotation Sensitivity Values (ASVs)\n  # =============================================\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"ASV framework: formal proofs for confounding, mediation, collider\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    details: >\n      Derive ASV expressions for 3 priority topologies.\n      Formal proofs of: (a) monotonicity (ASV increases with δ amplification),\n      (b) sharpness (bound is achievable for some confusion matrix).\n      MC validation: coverage at 90%, 95%, 99% levels across 1000 scenarios.\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"ASV MC validation for M-bias, instrument, front-door topologies\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_004]\n    details: >\n      ASV expressions + MC validation of monotonicity and coverage.\n      Sharpness stated as conjectures supported by numerical evidence.\n      If any topology fails monotonicity under MC, flag and investigate.\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"ASV calibration on empirical data (3 CSS tasks × 3 LLMs)\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_003, plan_004]\n    details: >\n      Apply ASVs to empirical confusion matrices from plan_003.\n      Validate coverage on held-out gold-standard splits.\n      Report ASV alongside downstream effect estimates for each task.\n      Compare ASV interpretability with raw confusion matrix reporting.\n\n  # =============================================\n  # Claim 3: Correction guidance framework\n  # =============================================\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    claim: 3\n    description: \"Correction guidance framework: decision mapping + validation\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_004, plan_003]\n    details: >\n      Decision framework: {topology × error structure × ASV} → correction method\n      (DSL / PPI / MLA / naive plug-in / \"no existing method adequate\").\n      MC validation: recommended method produces least bias in ≥90% of scenarios.\n      Empirical validation on plan_003 data.\n      Characterize regimes where no existing method suffices (correlated errors,\n      differential multi-class, etc.) — identify as open problems.\n\n  # =============================================\n  # Robustness / Ablation\n  # =============================================\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Pathological confusion matrix analysis (near-permutation, rank-deficient)\"\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    details: >\n      Extreme C structures: near-permutation, rank-deficient, block-diagonal.\n      Characterize when bias becomes catastrophic across topologies.\n      Identify structural conditions (spectral gap, diagonal dominance ratio)\n      that predict bias severity — candidate features for practitioners.\n\n  # =============================================\n  # Software / Reproducibility\n  # =============================================\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n    description: \"annot-sensitivity Python toolkit (open-source release)\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_004, plan_007]\n    details: >\n      Package: user-specified DAG + confusion matrix(es) + downstream estimate →\n      bias expressions (scalar K≤3, matrix K>3 with interpretability) +\n      ASV bounds + sensitivity curves + correction recommendation + diagnostic plots.\n      pip-installable, with worked examples for each topology.\n","numLines":148,"startLine":1,"totalLines":148}}}
